      "Language": "ita",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A controlled double-blind clinical trial using randomised blocks was carried out on 3 groups of 10 patients with internal diseases and a pain syndrome accompanied by anxiety. One group received the product under examination (FC 35aA) and the other two its components (dipotassic chlorazepate, paracetamol and codeine). FC 35aA gave the best results, pointing to synergism between its components. Increase of the pain threshold and of the actual involvement of the patient was achieved to an extent that the single components could not match when administered individually at the same doses."},
